  "decisions": [
    "A link-derived .. that leaves a granted directory continues from that directory's host parent when the remaining path spells out a granted directory; nothing outside the mounts is looked up. Paths that pass through an ungranted directory stay outside-root (known difference from PHP).",
    "Windows junctions are resolved as absolute link targets; mount path comparison folds case on Windows only.",
    "The 64-bit reference profile is (width, architecture, system): PHP 8.5.12 built with Apple clang for macOS amd64 initializes the left lazy comparison operand first, unlike linux/amd64.",
    "execution.write keeps its own copy of the output op: both ways of sharing it with writeTo measured slower on linux/amd64.",
    "ConfigError.Diagnostic uses the code's title as the message and the reason as the span label."
  ],
  "local_status": "pass",
  "product_test_status": "not_run",
